title: No confidence vote against the new government
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] faces a vote of no confidence.
new-page: true
view-if: bruning_event_timer = 5 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and (kvp_formed or traditionalist_split_2) and not bourgeois_coalition >= 50 and not concord_formed
on-arrival: bruning_event_seen = 1; judicial_reform -= 1
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= Vote of no confidence

Following the collapse of our coalition, President [+ president +] has appointed Heinrich Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Party in a government supported by bourgeois forces. However, they cannot survive without the support from us or Mallin's <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.

Askew, has reorganized his cabinet to include the parties to the right of the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not lvp_formed and not gold_exist: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?], such as the new <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, which has been granted generous cabinet positions. We are left with the choice to "tolerate" the government to prevent the gains of extremists within the Assembly or vote to oust Askew for new elections.

- @vote_no
- @vote_yes
- @no_matter

@vote_no
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire >= 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 3; bruning_event_timer = 0; unionist_relation -= 5
call: set_next_election_time

We have broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, and have voted against them in a vote of no confidence. We also repealed their emergency powers.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@vote_yes
title: Oppose the vote of no confidence, voting for the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a bourgeois government.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire >= 50
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; commons_marcher *= 0.9; disfavored_marcher *= 0.9; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 5; commons_royalist += 5; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_marcher -= 4 if welfare < 0; disfavored_marcher -= 5 if welfare < 0; pro_republic -= 4; collectivist_relation -= 8; landed_kvp += 3; landed_traditionalist -= 3; guild_kvp += 3; guild_traditionalist -= 3; burgher_kvp += 3; burgher_traditionalist -= 3; marcher_toleration_kvp = 1

We try to convince the workers that this policy is necessary in order to maintain a stable parliamentary government, and to deal with the fiscal consequences of the depression. Still, this policy provides excellent recruiting fodder for <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>. 

The <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> bolster their credentials against Mallin's "all or nothing" policy.

@no_matter
title: It does not matter what we do.
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote, no matter our choices.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire < 50
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5; bruning_event_timer = 0

The bourgeois coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].